ScamShield — project brief
Product

ScamShield protects older adults from scams by bringing their family into the moment of decision. Domain: scamshield.tech.

Senior = "Nani". Her side is a DESKTOP app built by teammate Kale in /desktop (C# WPF, .NET 8). On Shree-Branch never edit /desktop. On Shreekale, integration changes to /desktop are allowed: keep them in small, separate new files where possible and leave Kale's existing logic intact.
Family = Aarav (grandson) and Priya (daughter). They use the mobile web app at /family.
Community = /community dashboard of live scam campaigns in Atlanta.
The demo climax: a voice-cloned "grandson" calls Nani on WhatsApp → Kale's app detects it → Aarav's phone shows "Is this you?" → he taps NOT me → Nani is told to hang up → her $500 gift-card payment is held → Priya declines it.
Pitch line: "Every scam says 'don't tell anyone.' ScamShield makes sure you do."
The owner is not a software engineer
After every task, explain what you did in 2 plain-English sentences, and tell me exactly how to see it (URL/page).
Prefer simple, readable code. Small files. Clear names. No clever abstractions.
Before running a command that installs, deletes, or deploys, say what it does in one line.
Never commit secrets. Keys live in web/.env.local (gitignored) and in Vercel environment variables.
Work one step at a time; don't start the next feature unless asked.
Git: commit and push only to Shree-Branch (web-only work) or Shreekale (integration of web + Kale's desktop app). Never push to main or to Kale's branch, and never delete anything from Shree-Branch. Only switch or merge branches when the owner asks. Before any commit, run `git branch --show-current` and stop if it isn't one of those two.
Before building any UI, read docs/DESIGN_SPEC.md and follow it exactly.
Build work follows docs/BUILD_PLAN.md — execute only the phase I ask for, then stop.
Stack (don't change without asking)
Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS, in the folder web/.
Server = Next.js API routes in web/app/api/**/route.ts. Deployed on Vercel.
Database: MongoDB Atlas via the official mongodb driver, with a cached client in web/lib/db.ts. Database name "kin".
Charts: Recharts. Map: maplibre-gl with style https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty (client-only component).
Icons: lucide-react. Fonts: next/font/google (Fraunces + Inter).
All data shapes and endpoints MUST follow contract/CONTRACT.md exactly. Kale's desktop app depends on it.
Add CORS headers (allow all origins) on every /api route.
Design system — "Warm Sentinel"

Feeling: calm, human, trustworthy. A well-made banking app crossed with a family photo album. Never alarmist: no flashing, no red walls. Red only for critical/held.

